<article class="env-lemma" id="0CVM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CVM">Lemma <span data-tag="0CVM">77.7.5</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/083F" data-tag="083F">77.7.1</a> suppose given an exact sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F} \xrightarrow {u} \mathcal{G} \xrightarrow {v} \mathcal{H} \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> Then we have $F_{v, iso} = F_{u, zero}$ with obvious notation. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since pullback is right exact we see that $\mathcal{F}_ T \to \mathcal{G}_ T \to \mathcal{H}_ T \to 0$ is exact for every scheme $T$ over $B$. Hence $u_ T$ is surjective if and only if $v_ T$ is an isomorphism. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>